# A list: two strings in a row
#
# A list is things in a row, so you ask for one by its place, counting from
# zero. Here we ask for the first and the second, for one past the end, how
# many there are, and what the places are called.

## type
list
## len
2
## keys
0.0:int=0
0.1:int=1
## get .[0]
0.:str="lib/a.sh"
## get [1]
0.:str="test/a.bats"
## get .[7]

## has .[1]
true
## string .[0]
lib/a.sh
## scalar
!! 1 silt: not a scalar document, its first line: 0.0:str="lib/a.sh"
## get
0.0:str="lib/a.sh"
0.1:str="test/a.bats"
## each
0: 0.:str="lib/a.sh"
1: 0.:str="test/a.bats"
